<title>SWITZERLAND: 40,000 Rwandan refugees said fleeing E. Zaire camp.</title>
<headline>40,000 Rwandan refugees said fleeing E. Zaire camp.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 40,000 Rwandan refugees fled encampments in the Shabunda area of eastern Zaire on Wednesday following reports that rebels had taken a nearby town, the United Nations refugee agency (UNHCR) said.</p>
<p>Local authorities said the refugees moved out after reports swept through Shabunda that Katshunga, a small town located some 45 km (25 miles) northeast of Shabunda, had fallen. There was no independent confirmation of these reports, the UNHCR said in a statement released in Geneva.</p>
</text>
